  "problem": "Schema-valid model JSON could introduce unknown fields, citations or record IDs. Quote matching could be treated as scientific certification. Unsupported claims could be retried until a preferred answer appeared. Accepted proposals could lack resolvable citations.",
  "resulting_behavior": "parseConstrainedExtraction requires field, value, passage IDs, quotation/span, claim type, uncertainty and abstention reason, limited to the requested task scope. Unknown field, citation or record ID fails even when JSON is syntactically valid. validateClaim checks quoted spans against immutable captures, flags a correct quote with the wrong semantic role for review, and never treats quote matching as scientific certification. Invented units/definitions and unresolvable citations are schema-valid hallucinations and fail. Unsupported claims remain rejected across reruns. Syntax/transport failures are retryable; unsupported claims are not. Accepted literals are traceable without calling the model again. 100% of accepted proposals have resolvable citations.",
